Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(spec):=20wire=20exclusion=20gate=20nel=20r?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ound=20concat=20+=20osservabilit=C3=A0=20[t8=20branch-2]?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Chunk 2 runtime, task 6: the per-round exclusion goes live. When a
round is about to become concat (MTP arm, k1 > 0, temp 0), the gate
reads the last W confirmed tokens ending at the anchor (dp.id_last @
dp.n_past, wiring map section 4.2) and, if the window is pattern-like,
routes the sequence down the PLAIN path for that round - the exact
k1 = 0 behavior: no head injection, no composed marker, no impl_head
attribution, mask-placeholder block. Ungated windows keep the concat
round unchanged; --no-spec-concat-exclusion skips the gate entirely
(A-noexclusion test arm); a k1 = 0 boot never reaches the gate
(structural inertia - bit-identical certification is G0, next task).

- speculative.cpp: the gate sits in the seq-classification branch of
  common_speculative_draft() BEFORE seq_concat admission (the head is
  published, and its injection armed, only through seq_concat); a
  gated round reuses the seq_routed stash - the same mechanism as the
  temp > 0 fallback and the k1 = 0 foreign-drafter path. Harness
  carries concat_exclusion + the TELEMETRY-ONLY cumulative counters
  (total/gated), printed next to the per-impl statistics block, only
  when k1 > 0 (no new output on k1 = 0 boots). process-MTP untouched.
- spec-concat-exclusion.h: gating_result gains p_best (DIAGNOSTIC
  ONLY - AC argmax lag if AC fired, else the constant-class period,
  -1 when not gated; NOT part of the fixture contract); new
  pointer+count+anchor overload gating(tok, n, last) delegating to
  the certified vector gating() - the runtime confirmed window is two
  pieces in the caller's buffers (prompt tail + id_last), so the
  wiring passes the tail by pointer without copying the slot buffer.
  has_constant_class() now delegates to constant_class_period() (the
  verbatim scan, returning the period) so decision and diagnostic
  twins cannot drift.
- observability: per-round gated log 'spec-concat: gated p=<p> segnale=
  <ac|classe|ac+classe>' at SPC_INF (the spec-route marker level,
  visible at the production -lv 3); boot marker nested inside the
  concat_ready guard now prints 'concat exclusion active
  (theta_ac=0.60 m=4 w=16)' with constants read from the detector
  header (task 5 review: a degraded dual boot no longer logs
  'concat mode disabled' next to an exclusion state line).
- arg.cpp (task 5 review): --spec-concat-selftest is server-only -
  llama-cli/speculative now reject it instead of accepting it
  silently; --spec-concat-exclusion stays a passive triple flag.

G1 re-run on the new image: selftest PASS 200/200 exit 0 (fixtures
and the gated+segnale contract unchanged).

